**How to implement.** The import seam reads what the library holds and writes whole entry versions, so an imported entry keeps its own version, provenance and hash (001 §B 'Per-entry import decision'; '`SeedingProxy` / `seedAll` become `CatalogueImport`: the same seam shape, fed from parsed files; the in-memory implementation stays as the test double'; the S3.1 brief: the apply function writes through the stores, and nothing else writes; S2.3 interpretation 9). In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs`: (1) `CatalogueImportError` keeps its three cases and gains `InvalidImportChoiceErr` (a choice whose action its row does not offer), `DanglingReferenceErr` (a written entry names an entry the same apply skips or re-binds) and `EntryHashingErr` (an entry could not be sealed), each `of reason : string` naming the entry. `describe` gains a line for each, in step 39's form. (2) `EntryVersionPut = { envelope : LibraryEntryEnvelope; latest : LatestMove }` is one version to store. (3) `CatalogueImportProxy` stays `[<ReferenceEquality>]`, and five fields replace its four save fields. `tryHeldEntry : LibraryEntryId -> Result<HeldEntry option, CatalogueImportError>` answers what the library holds for an id (step 93). `heldEntriesNamed : LibraryEntryKind -> EntryName -> Result<HeldEntry list, CatalogueImportError>` answers the held entries of the kind whose latest version has the name. `heldEntriesOf : CatalogueId -> Result<HeldEntry list, CatalogueImportError>` answers the held entries whose latest provenance is `BuiltInProvenance` of the catalogue. `putEntryVersion : EntryVersionPut -> Result<unit, CatalogueImportError>` stores the envelope as a version of its entry, `ActiveEntry` and unpinned. It becomes the entry's latest when the entry had none or the put says `MoveLatestVersion`. It answers `ImportRejectedErr` for a version the entry already holds and for an id held as another kind, so a put never overwrites. `retireEntry : LibraryEntryId -> Result<unit, CatalogueImportError>` marks the entry's latest version `InactiveEntry`; an id not held is `ImportRejectedErr`. The record's doc states this contract in one to three lines. (4) `ofStores` (step 80) keeps its signature and becomes the in-memory implementation of (3). A closure-local map, as in `CatalogueProxy.createInMemory` (`CatalogueFiles.fs`, step 32), holds each put entry's envelopes in ascending version order, its latest version and the lifecycle of that latest. The five fields read and write that map. A put of an id the map does not hold first decodes the envelope with its kind's decoder (step 25) and pushes the value through the store's write verb, as step 80's adapters do: `UndecodableEntryErr`, or `ImportRejectedErr` with the store's reason, stops the put before the map changes. So the four stores hold every new entry; a later version or a retirement is the seam's own. Its doc says so in one to three lines. `createInMemory ()` keeps its signature and body. (5) On the proxy, `member this.decideCatalogue (catalogue : CatalogueData) : Result<ImportDecision list, CatalogueImportError>` uses the origin `CatalogueImportOrigin (catalogue.manifest.id, catalogue.manifest.name)`. For each envelope, in row order, it calls `tryHeldEntry`. When that answers `None`, it calls `heldEntriesNamed` for the envelope's kind and name. It then calls `ImportDecision.decide` (step 93). Then each entry of `heldEntriesOf catalogue.manifest.id` that is `ActiveEntry` and named by no manifest row is `ImportDecision.unlisted`. The first read error stops it. (6) `[<ReferenceEquality>] CatalogueImportContext = { proxy : CatalogueImportProxy; sealEntry : LibraryEntryContent -> Result<LibraryEntryEnvelope, CatalogueImportError>; newEntryId : unit -> LibraryEntryId }` follows the `*Context` convention (AGENTS.md): the seam plus the providers that a fork needs. Domain does not hash (step 26), and the id is injected so that a test is deterministic. Three members: (a) `member this.apply (choices : ImportChoice list) : Result<ImportOutcome, CatalogueImportError>` uses `EntryRebinding = { incoming : LibraryEntryId; held : LibraryEntryId }`, `EntryFork = { original : LibraryEntryId; fork : LibraryEntryId }` and `ImportOutcome = { rebindings : EntryRebinding list; forks : EntryFork list }`. It first checks every choice: its action MUST be the row's `defaultAction` or one of its `alternatives`, else `InvalidImportChoiceErr`. A choice that writes its incoming entry (an add, a version or a fork) whose content's `referencedEntryIds` names the `entryId` of a choice that skips or re-binds is `DanglingReferenceErr` naming both. Nothing is written before these checks pass. It then writes in reference order: categories, materials, samples, sources, polarizers and detectors, in choice order within a kind, with every `RetireHeldEntry` last. `AddIncomingEntry` puts the envelope with `MoveLatestVersion`, and `AddIncomingVersion move` puts it with `move`. `ForkIncomingEntry` takes the incoming content with `id = newEntryId ()`, `version = VersionNumber.first` and `provenance = ForkProvenance { originalId; originalVersion; originalProvenance }` of the incoming content (step 91). It seals that content through `sealEntry`, puts it with `MoveLatestVersion`, and records the `EntryFork`. `RebindToHeldEntry h` records the `EntryRebinding` and writes nothing. `ReuseHeldEntry` and `SkipIncomingEntry` write nothing. `RetireHeldEntry` calls `retireEntry`. The first failure stops the apply, and the writes before it stay (step 40's rule). (b) `member this.importCatalogue (catalogue : CatalogueData) : Result<ImportDecision list, CatalogueImportError>` MUST run `decideCatalogue` and return every row, without calling `apply` or writing any entry. The caller MUST confirm the complete choice list before `apply` (.spec-md §3.7). (c) `member this.importFrom (catalogue : CatalogueProxy) : Result<ImportDecision list, CatalogueImportError>` reads it (`CatalogueUnreadableErr`) and imports it. The proxy's `importCatalogue` and `importFrom` (step 40) are deleted, because these replace them. (7) New `OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueImportStore.fs`, `module CatalogueImportStore` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Storage`, compiled directly after `LibraryBackupStore.fs` (step 86), with one `<Compile>` line and no comment. It holds `type CatalogueImportContext with static member create (proxy : CatalogueImportProxy) : CatalogueImportContext`. Its `sealEntry` is `LibraryEntryContent.sealed` (step 30), mapping a `StorageError` to `EntryHashingErr` with its `describe`. Its `newEntryId` mints a new GUID. Its doc is one line citing spec 0050 S3.1. (8) Callers. `BuiltinCatalogue.freshStores ()` (step 41) imports the loaded catalogue through `(CatalogueImportContext.create stores.proxy).importCatalogue`. The test fixture MUST explicitly confirm all returned defaults through `apply` before answering the stores; any error MUST fail the fixture with its diagnostic. `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:DefaultStores.create` (steps 42, 58) imports through `(CatalogueImportContext.create stores.proxy).importFrom (CatalogueProxy.createBuiltIn ())`; an `Error e` is logged as today. `OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs`' compose (steps 88, 89) imports into a created database through `(CatalogueImportContext.create (CatalogueImportProxy.ofStores …)).importFrom`, over the same stores and catalogue as today. Production composition MUST retain the returned decisions without applying defaults; the startup report and Launcher handoff consume them in steps 98–112. The test-only DefaultStores and all test fixtures MUST explicitly apply their chosen defaults, so test setup is deliberate confirmation, not production startup policy. No retry, cache, option or other field is added. (9) Tests. In `CatalogueImportProxyTests`, `recordingProxy` holds an empty library: `tryHeldEntry` answers `None`, both lists answer `[]`, and it records every put and retirement on its tape, refusing a put when the fact's predicate says so. Its facts drive `CatalogueImportContext.create` over it, with `newEntryId` replaced by a fixed test-local id. `importCatalogue pushes every entry once, categories then materials then samples then presets, through the exact signatures`: the tape is every category envelope, then every material, sample, source, polarizer and detector envelope, each put once with `MoveLatestVersion`, in row order within a kind. `importCatalogue stops at the first rejected entry and answers its ImportRejectedErr`: refusing every material leaves every category put and nothing else. `every import error renders its condition and its payload` covers the three new cases. `a CatalogueImportProxy compares by reference (the [<ReferenceEquality>] contract)` holds over the new proxy. The class gains three facts. `apply refuses an action its row does not offer, and a write that would leave a reference dangling, before it writes`: a choice of `ReuseHeldEntry` on an `EntryIdNotHeld` row answers `InvalidImportChoiceErr`, and a sample added while its material is skipped answers `DanglingReferenceErr`; in both cases the tape stays empty. `apply forks a divergent entry under a minted id whose provenance keeps the original`: the one put is the fixed id at version 1, under `ForkProvenance` of the original's id, version and provenance, with the hash that `sealed` gives that content, and the outcome names the fork. `apply writes nothing for a reuse, a skip or a re-binding, answers the binding, and retires after every put`: over a retired row, an add, a reuse, a skip and a re-binding, given in that order, the tape holds the add's put and then the retirement, and the outcome holds the one re-binding. `an entry that does not decode stops the import with UndecodableEntryErr` moves to `CatalogueImportInMemoryTests`, over `CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory ()`, because only the in-memory double decodes: the import answers `UndecodableEntryErr (MissingEntryFieldErr _)` after the category alone is put. `CatalogueImportInMemoryTests`' other facts import through `CatalogueImportContext.create` of `createInMemory ()`'s proxy and keep their assertions. `importing a catalogue the stores already hold is refused` becomes `importing a catalogue the stores already hold reuses every entry and writes nothing`: a second `importCatalogue` through the same context MUST answer every `SameContentHash` row, whose explicitly confirmed defaults write nothing, and every store lists what it listed. `LibraryDatabaseTests`' `importFrom fills an empty library database through the database stores` imports through `CatalogueImportContext.create` over `ofStores` of the four database stores. Its second import through the same context MUST return every reuse row; explicitly applying their defaults MUST leave the stores unchanged. All tape, failure and decoded-entry assertions in this step MUST call `importCatalogue`/`importFrom` to obtain the complete rows, assert the tape is empty, and then explicitly `apply` the chosen defaults before asserting writes or the first write error. Test fixture imports MUST use that same two-phase sequence; no production helper MAY confirm for a user. TestAppScope.freshAppContext and the AppContextTests population fixtures MUST explicitly confirm the complete default choices returned by importFrom after creating their database context. Tests asserting startup identification MUST retain the unconfirmed context instead. These test-only callers MUST be updated together with the import seam.

**Acceptance.** After the seam is reshaped, `CatalogueImportProxy` MUST declare `tryHeldEntry`, `heldEntriesNamed`, `heldEntriesOf`, `putEntryVersion` and `retireEntry` and no save field, and `CatalogueImportContext` MUST declare `apply`, `importCatalogue` and `importFrom`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `apply refuses an action its row does not offer, and a write that would leave a reference dangling, before it writes`, `apply forks a divergent entry under a minted id whose provenance keeps the original`, `apply writes nothing for a reuse, a skip or a re-binding, answers the binding, and retires after every put`, `an entry that does not decode stops the import with UndecodableEntryErr` and `importing a catalogue the stores already hold reuses every entry and writes nothing`, the count rising by 3; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the eleven s12 invariants MUST pass. All import rows, including Reuse, MUST require explicit confirmation before library or import-log mutation; an unchanged catalogue manifest or a kit with no snapshots is the only applicable bypass.
